Azyr #36 / #41 extracted-source checks
=====================================

From the kernel root:

    python3 tools/testing/selftests/cpufreq_ipa/test_tuning.py \
        --self-test-negatives --general-regs-only

Requires Python 3, git, GCC (or --cc with a compatible host compiler) and its
UBSan runtime. --general-regs-only is optional and compiler/host dependent.
No downloads, kernel builds or hardware execution. Intentional assertion-failure
controls have core dumps disabled.

Checks the exact two-source patch/inverse and reviewed preimage hashes. For IPA,
extracts the real delay declaration/call/macro, checks 10000..12000 microseconds
with integer arithmetic, and verifies that restoring just this change reproduces
the entire original IPA file. For cpufreq, extracts both versions of the actual
transition function and checks 180 combinations covering absent stats, initial
invalid index, invalid new frequency, unchanged index and valid transitions.
Checks last index, update count, total transitions and the entire transition
matrix. Compiled mutants changing the minimum, removing slack and breaking the
unchanged-index guard must fail assertions.

These are host mocks with UBSan, not a production AOSP target build or proof of
real timer coalescing, concurrent cpufreq behavior, modem/WLAN stability, device
boot, latency, performance or power gains. See the application record:

    Documentation/dev-tools/azyr-sm6250-036-041-validation.json
    Documentation/dev-tools/azyr-sm6250-036-041-validation.txt
    Documentation/dev-tools/azyr-sm6250-036-041.diff
